message: "If you cite this computational research thesis, please use the metadata below. No DOI is minted here; do not invent one."
type: thesis
title: "Composing named observation channels into a Disease Profile without illegal merge into Θ"
authors:
  - family-names: Ogbonna
    given-names: Kelechi Emeka
    email: kelechiogbonna300@gmail.com
    alias: cloudynirvana
abstract: >-
  When do separately named observation channels compose into a Disease
  Profile without illegally merging into a single therapeutic parameter θ?
  The legal operator is disjoint union of named maps. Identification, a
  product, an arithmetic mean, promotion of one coefficient into θ, a
  repeated channel identifier, and a cross-class join are refused. On a
  five-preparation linear toy the joint Fisher rank is 3. The identified
  symbol is a design-weighted average and matches none of the generating
  coefficients. A product of two coefficients has a flat profile along the
  hyperbola. Not a medical device. No assay table is copied. No document DOI.
keywords:
  - observation channel
  - disease profile
  - composition
  - disjoint union
  - profile likelihood
  - Fisher information
  - identifiability
  - research-only
